<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner-small splatFont"><span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize 'wod.health.health'}}</span></div>	
<!--<div>Vänsterklick att lägga till skada, högerklick rensar aktuell ruta.</div>-->

<div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
    <div>{{getInjuredLevel actor.type actor.system.health actor.system.health.damage}}</div>
</div>
    
<div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
    {{!-- TWO DEFECTS THIS LOOP EXPOSED, both in the code it replaced.

          1. `wounded` HAD NO `data-type` AT ALL — a blank line where the other six had it. That
             attribute is the SWITCH in `OnSquareCounterChange` (action-helpers.js): `mortal` writes
             `health.damage`, `changeling` writes `health.damage.chimerical`, `wraith` writes
             `health.damage.corpus`. With it undefined NO branch matched, so clicking the Wounded
             box recorded nothing — on both sheets, for every character. The loop cannot reproduce a
             per-level omission, so it is fixed here; that is a behaviour change and a deliberate one.

          2. The two tracks pass DIFFERENT sheettypes — `mortal` here, `changeling` below — and a
             first draft of this loop hardcoded `mortal` for both. That would have made a click on a
             chimerical box write to the character's REAL health. Caught by diffing the rendered
             markup against the pre-refactor file, not by reading. --}}
    {{!-- redesign-health-track 3.1 — ONE loop over `config.woundLevels`, not seven copies.
          `config` is `CONFIG.worldofdarkness` (pc-actor-sheet.js:320), so the level list comes from
          the same place `totals.js` iterates when it computes `.total` — add a level there and it
          appears here, instead of needing an eighth copy of this block in two tracks.
          `@root` is used for `config` and the damage-state array rather than counting `../`: the
          body sits inside `#each` > `#with` > `#numLoop`, and `numLoop` is a CUSTOM block helper
          whose depth behaviour is not something to re-derive at every edit. `lvl` is a block
          parameter, which stays in lexical scope through all three. --}}
    {{#each config.woundLevels as |lbl lvl|}}
        {{#with (lookup @root.actor.system.health lvl)}}
            {{#if (gt total 0)}}

        <div class="health">
            <div class="resource-counter healthbox" data-name="data.system.health.{{lvl}}">
                {{#numLoop total}}
                    <span class="resource-value-step healthBox {{lvl}}" 
                        data-type="{{@root.config.sheettype.mortal}}"
                        data-action="editHealth"
                        data-index="{{this}}" 
                        data-state="{{damageState ../label @root.health this}}"></span>            
                {{/numLoop}}
            </div>
        </div>

            {{/if}}
        {{/with}}
    {{/each}}
</div>

{{#if actor.system.settings.usechimerical}}

    <div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner-small splatFont"><span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize 'wod.health.chimerical'}}</span></div>

    <div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
        <div>{{getInjuredLevel actor.type actor.system.health actor.system.health.damage.chimerical}}</div>
    </div>

    <div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
    {{!-- redesign-health-track 3.1 — ONE loop over `config.woundLevels`, not seven copies.
          `config` is `CONFIG.worldofdarkness` (pc-actor-sheet.js:320), so the level list comes from
          the same place `totals.js` iterates when it computes `.total` — add a level there and it
          appears here, instead of needing an eighth copy of this block in two tracks.
          `@root` is used for `config` and the damage-state array rather than counting `../`: the
          body sits inside `#each` > `#with` > `#numLoop`, and `numLoop` is a CUSTOM block helper
          whose depth behaviour is not something to re-derive at every edit. `lvl` is a block
          parameter, which stays in lexical scope through all three. --}}
    {{#each config.woundLevels as |lbl lvl|}}
        {{#with (lookup @root.actor.system.health lvl)}}
            {{#if (gt total 0)}}

        <div class="health">
            <div class="resource-counter healthbox" data-name="data.system.health.{{lvl}}">
                {{#numLoop total}}
                    <span class="resource-value-step healthBox {{lvl}}" 
                        data-type="{{@root.config.sheettype.changeling}}"
                        data-action="editHealth"
                        data-index="{{this}}" 
                        data-state="{{damageState ../label @root.chimericalhealth this}}"></span>            
                {{/numLoop}}
            </div>
        </div>

            {{/if}}
        {{/with}}
    {{/each}}
    </div>

{{/if}}

{{!--
    add-wraith-pc-splat §3.3 — the Corpus track.

    Deliberately NOT a second copy of the health ladder above, and the rules are explicit about why: a
    wraith "pierde Corpus EN LUGAR DE niveles de Salud a razón de uno por uno"
    (wraith20-el-olvido-nsr-es L6811). So there are no wound-level names, and there is **no penalty line** —
    a wraith takes no dice or movement penalty from Corpus damage at all (L10581).

    The track is as long as PERMANENT Corpus (L10543: permanent is the maximum, temporary fluctuates and
    can never exceed it), which is exactly the length of the array `calculateHealth`'s wraith branch
    returns — every entry with `label: ""`.

    The three marks are the book's own ("/" bashing, "x" lethal, "*" aggravated; bashing escalates by
    marking a second line into an X, L10611-10613). They matter for WHICH STATE a full track puts the
    wraith in, not for penalties: all bashing -> Vacilante (L10577); lethal -> Atormentado and an immediate
    Harrowing (L10583). Neither is automated — both are Storyteller calls with a Willpower-vs-Angst roll.
    Healing is 1 Pathos for 2 bashing or 1 lethal, max one Pathos per turn (L10635).
--}}
{{#if corpushealth}}

    <div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner-small splatFont"><span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize 'wod.advantages.corpus'}}</span></div>

    <div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
        <div class="health">
            <div class="resource-counter healthbox" data-name="data.system.health.damage.corpus">
                {{#numLoop corpushealth.length}}
                    <span class="resource-value-step healthBox"
                        data-type="{{../config.sheettype.wraith}}"
                        data-action="editHealth"
                        data-index="{{this}}"
                        data-state="{{damageState "" ../corpushealth this}}"></span>
                {{/numLoop}}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

{{/if}}

<div class="sheet-boxcontainer">
    <div class="information-area">{{localize "wod.health.penalty"}}: {{ignorePain actor.system.health.damage.woundpenalty}}</div>    
</div>